{
  "_comment": [
    "The composter's shell: a 2px floor and four 2px walls, leaving a 12x12 well open at the top.",
    "The only difference is what the inside face is -- a canvas screen rather than a plank bottom,",
    "because the screen is the whole point of the block and the open top is the only place it can be",
    "seen.",
    "",
    "The outer faces are a coopered tub (staves and two iron hoops) rather than a slatted crate, and",
    "that is load-bearing rather than decorative: this block holds a bucket of water when it runs as",
    "an Ice-o-lator, and a crate visibly would not.",
    "",
    "Hand-written rather than datagen'd for the same reason the two machines are: no model provider",
    "expresses a five-element shell, and the blockstate that goes with it is multipart."
  ],
